{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Pjcu8LDf2TLFrKBnEJEYVC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for each planned experiment in the experiment plan, assuming the \"best\" tier outcome. I need to provide realistic, detailed predictions with rationales for why these results would occur in the best-case scenario for an EMNLP Main submission.\n\nLet me carefully go through each experiment and generate predictions consistent with the best tier definition.\n\nBest tier means:\n- ≥2 additional benchmarks show significant convergence (Spearman p<0.05)\n- 7B models available and convergence deepens\n- Excluding GDN doesn't change conclusions\n- Per-example Jaccard < 0.10 across multiple tasks\n\n\n- ≥2 features significantly distinguish helped/hurt samples\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected metric ranges for these best-case outcomes—tasks with significant convergence spanning 3-5, substantial standard deviation reductions of 70-90%, strong negative correlations around -0.9 to -1.0 for the 1.3B model, minimal overlap in affected samples with Jaccard distances under 0.08, and clear feature distinctions emerging from 2-4 significant characteristics.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c735bf5f-f1ac-4fff-bfc2-71786796f636","uuid":"38b50d23-4e63-4876-a432-2881e3a87966"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Pjcu8LDf2TLFrKBnEJEYVC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  三条claims全部保留，title直接用\"The Equalizer Effect\"。\n  叙事主线：attention作为universal equalizer跨任务跨scale生效，但per-example机制architecture-specific。\n  7B三点scale curve完成monotonic convergence story。\n  多任务覆盖（LAMBADA+HellaSwag+ARC-e）消除task-specificity质疑。\n  与Wang et al.形成清晰互补：他们提供model zoo，我们揭示他们遗漏的深层现象。\n  目标EMNLP 2026 Main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Cross-task convergence quantification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对6个benchmark在1.3B和340M两个scale上计算cross-architecture std随attention ratio变化趋势，\n      Spearman rank correlation检验convergence显著性，按retrieval-dependent vs reasoning-dependent分类。\n    expected_results:\n      tasks_with_significant_convergence_1_3b: 4\n      lambada_spearman_rho: -1.0\n      lambada_spearman_p: 0.0083\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 79\n      hellaswag_spearman_rho: -0.90\n      hellaswag_spearman_p: 0.037\n      arc_easy_spearman_rho: -0.95\n      arc_easy_spearman_p: 0.017\n      winogrande_spearman_rho: -0.90\n      winogrande_spearman_p: 0.037\n      piqa_spearman_rho: -0.50\n      piqa_spearman_p: 0.391\n      arc_challenge_spearman_rho: -0.60\n      arc_challenge_spearman_p: 0.285\n      retrieval_tasks_avg_rho: -0.94\n      reasoning_tasks_avg_rho: -0.55\n      task_type_dichotomy_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA是纯retrieval任务（从context中提取最后一词），convergence最强（ρ=-1.0）已被现有数据确认。\n      HellaSwag（commonsense continuation选择）和ARC-e（简单科学问答）均有较强的context-grounding成分，\n      attention层通过增强context integration使不同recurrence机制的弱点得到互补性修正，因此也会出现显著convergence。\n      Winogrande（共指消解）需要精确的long-range reference resolution，这恰好是attention的强项，\n      因此也会出现convergence。PIQA和ARC-challenge更依赖reasoning和world knowledge而非retrieval，\n      不同recurrence机制在这些任务上的差异更多来自训练动态而非architecture capacity gap，\n      attention无法系统性地弥合这类差异，convergence不显著。\n      这形成了清晰的task-type dichotomy：retrieval-dependent任务convergence显著，reasoning任务不显著。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Task Type\", \"Std(attn=0)\", \"Std(attn=8)\", \"Reduction%\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"retrieval\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\", -1.00, 0.0083]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"retrieval-grounded\", 0.018, 0.007, \"61%\", -0.90, 0.037]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"retrieval-grounded\", 0.031, 0.011, \"65%\", -0.95, 0.017]\n          - [\"Winogrande\", \"coreference\", 0.022, 0.009, \"59%\", -0.90, 0.037]\n          - [\"PIQA\", \"reasoning\", 0.015, 0.011, \"27%\", -0.50, 0.391]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"reasoning\", 0.028, 0.019, \"32%\", -0.60, 0.285]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 1: 六个benchmark的cross-arch std vs attention ratio折线图（1.3B），\n        retrieval类任务用实线（显示clear monotonic decrease），reasoning类用虚线（flat或noisy）。\n        双panel：左1.3B右340M，340M panel显示rebound现象。\n    analysis: >\n      4个任务显著convergence超出pass_fail阈值（≥2），且task-type dichotomy清晰。\n      retrieval-dependent任务的convergence可用attention的context integration功能解释：\n      不同recurrence机制各有retrieval盲区，attention统一补偿这些盲区。\n      reasoning任务的non-convergence支持\"equalizer effect is retrieval-specific\"的refined claim，\n      这比\"universal convergence\"更有趣——说明attention的equalizing作用有边界条件。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对1.3B模型在HellaSwag、ARC-easy、ARC-challenge上用--log_samples重新跑lm-eval，\n      提取per-example accuracy变化，计算cross-architecture helped/hurt overlap（Jaccard），\n      验证equalizer paradox是否在LAMBADA之外复现。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_mean: 0.06\n      arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_mean: 0.07\n      arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_mean: 0.12\n      hellaswag_helped_pct_gdn: 0.18\n      hellaswag_helped_pct_retnet: 0.21\n      hellaswag_helped_pct_hgrn2: 0.19\n      hellaswag_hurt_pct_gdn: 0.14\n      hellaswag_hurt_pct_retnet: 0.11\n      hellaswag_hurt_pct_hgrn2: 0.09\n      paradox_replicated_hellaswag: true\n      paradox_replicated_arc_easy: true\n      paradox_replicated_arc_challenge: false\n      gpu_hours_actual: 7.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      HellaSwag和ARC-e在exp-001中显示显著aggregate convergence，per-example分析将揭示\n      这种convergence也是通过non-overlapping sample subsets实现的（Jaccard<0.10），\n      因为不同recurrence机制的context建模弱点在不同样本上显现：\n      GDN的gated delta rule在需要precise memory update的样本上弱，\n      RetNet的exponential decay在long-range dependency样本上弱，\n      HGRN2的hierarchical gating在需要flat attention分布的样本上弱。\n      Attention分别修补这些不同的弱点，因此affected samples几乎不重叠。\n      ARC-challenge因为aggregate convergence本身不显著，per-example pattern也更noisy，\n      Jaccard略高但paradox不clean。\n      这个结果直接强化Claim 3：equalizer paradox不是LAMBADA的artifact，\n      而是retrieval-grounded任务的general phenomenon。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-example overlap across benchmarks (Jaccard index, 1.3B, h3-1 vs h0)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"GDN-RetNet\", \"GDN-HGRN2\", \"RetNet-HGRN2\", \"Mean Jaccard\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", 0.04, 0.05, 0.03, 0.04]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", 0.07, 0.06, 0.05, 0.06]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", 0.08, 0.07, 0.06, 0.07]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", 0.14, 0.11, 0.12, 0.12]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 2: 三个benchmark的Venn diagram（或UpSet plot），展示三个architecture的helped samples重叠。\n        每个benchmark一个panel，清晰显示重叠区域极小。\n      - >\n        Figure 3: Per-example effect heatmap——行为样本，列为architecture，\n        颜色编码accuracy变化方向和幅度，显示\"棋盘格\"pattern（非一致方向）。\n    analysis: >\n      Equalizer paradox在LAMBADA、HellaSwag、ARC-e三个任务上复现，\n      mean Jaccard均<0.10，满足best tier的pass_fail标准。\n      这是论文的核心contribution加强版：paradox不是task-specific artifact，\n      而是attention介入retrieval-dependent任务的general mechanism。\n      ARC-challenge的higher Jaccard提供了有趣的boundary condition讨论。\n\n  - name: \"7B model evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      从Wang et al. HuggingFace repos获取7B-scale models，\n      在6个benchmark上评估，构建3-scale (340M, 1.3B, 7B) convergence trajectory。\n    expected_results:\n      models_available_7b: 3\n      architectures_available_7b: [\"GatedDeltaNet\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_7b_h0: 0.019\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_7b_h3_1: 0.002\n      lambada_std_reduction_7b_pct: 89\n      hellaswag_std_reduction_7b_pct: 75\n      arc_easy_std_reduction_7b_pct: 71\n      scale_convergence_spearman_rho: -1.0\n      scale_convergence_spearman_p: 0.0083\n      monotonic_deepening_confirmed: true\n      gpu_hours_actual: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的model zoo包含多scale实验，7B是他们的largest scale，极可能有模型。\n      在best tier下，7B模型可获取且convergence继续deepening的原因：\n      (1) 更大的模型capacity使attention层的context integration更充分，\n      各recurrence机制的residual差异被更有效地弥合；\n      (2) 7B的training dynamics更稳定，340M的rebound现象（capacity不足导致attention和recurrence争抢参数）\n      在7B上消失；\n      (3) 三点scale curve (340M partial → 1.3B strong → 7B near-complete)\n      形成clean monotonic trajectory，std reduction从~40% → ~79% → ~89%，\n      支持\"convergence随scale增强\"的narrative。\n      这完成了Claim 2的scale story，从binary contrast升级为三点趋势线。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Cross-architecture std across scales\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"Attn Config\", \"LAMBADA Std\", \"HellaSwag Std\", \"ARC-E Std\", \"Mean Std (retrieval tasks)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"340M\", \"h0\", 0.021, 0.016, 0.028, 0.022]\n          - [\"340M\", \"h3-1\", 0.013, 0.012, 0.020, 0.015]\n          - [\"1.3B\", \"h0\", 0.024, 0.018, 0.031, 0.024]\n          - [\"1.3B\", \"h3-1\", 0.005, 0.007, 0.011, 0.008]\n          - [\"7B\", \"h0\", 0.019, 0.015, 0.025, 0.020]\n          - [\"7B\", \"h3-1\", 0.002, 0.004, 0.007, 0.004]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4: 三点scale curve——x轴为model scale (340M, 1.3B, 7B)，\n        y轴为cross-arch std (h3-1 config)，三条线分别对应LAMBADA、HellaSwag、ARC-e。\n        所有线monotonically decrease，LAMBADA下降最陡。\n        右侧secondary y轴显示std reduction percentage。\n    analysis: >\n      7B数据的获取和monotonic deepening是best tier的关键区分因素。\n      三点curve使Claim 2从\"two-point contrast\"升级为\"scaling law\"，\n      可以拟合power law或log-linear关系，增强理论深度。\n      7B的near-complete convergence（LAMBADA std仅0.002）暗示\n      在sufficient scale下attention几乎完全消除architecture差异，\n      这对architecture selection有直接practical implication。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析340M在attn=8时的non-monotonic rebound，\n      per-example比较340M和1.3B在相同attention ratio下的差异，\n      识别rebound的根本原因。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_magnitude_std_increase: 0.006\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 0.45\n      capacity_bottleneck_confirmed: true\n      rebound_correlated_with_context_length: true\n      rebound_context_length_threshold: 85\n      rebound_explained_variance_by_capacity: 0.62\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M的rebound在attn=8时出现，这是最高attention ratio。\n      在best tier下，机制将被清晰识别为capacity bottleneck：\n      340M总参数有限，当attention层占比过高时recurrence层的参数被过度压缩，\n      导致recurrence的sequence modeling能力退化。\n      表现为长context样本（>85 tokens）上的性能下降，\n      因为这些样本本来最依赖recurrence的sequential processing。\n      1.3B不出现rebound是因为总capacity足够同时支撑attention和recurrence。\n      这个发现完美补充scale story：convergence需要sufficient scale，\n      不仅是scale越大convergence越深，而且scale不足时会出现pathological behavior。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: 340M rebound characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Rebound Samples\", \"Non-rebound Samples\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Mean context length (tokens)\", 112.3, 68.7, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"Target token frequency rank\", 4521, 3890, 0.23]\n          - [\"Overlap with 1.3B hurt samples\", \"45%\", \"12%\", \"<0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 5: 340M vs 1.3B的per-example effect scatter plot，\n        x轴为1.3B上的accuracy change，y轴为340M上的accuracy change。\n        颜色编码context length，长context样本聚集在340M negative / 1.3B positive象限。\n    analysis: >\n      Capacity bottleneck解释简洁且可验证，为scale-dependent convergence提供mechanistic grounding。\n      长context样本在340M上的rebound可以解释为：recurrence层capacity不足以维持long-range state，\n      而attention层虽然能做long-range retrieval但在340M上head数量不足以覆盖所有位置。\n      这个发现增加了论文的理论深度，不仅是描述性的\"scale matters\"，而是解释性的\"why scale matters\"。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对LAMBADA上每个architecture的helped/hurt samples计算linguistic features：\n      target token frequency, context length, last-sentence perplexity, topic distribution，\n      检验feature是否显著区分helped vs hurt，以及feature profile是否跨architecture不同。\n    expected_results:\n      significant_features_count: 3\n      target_token_frequency_p_value: 0.003\n      context_length_p_value: 0.001\n      last_sentence_perplexity_p_value: 0.008\n      topic_distribution_p_value: 0.12\n      gdn_hurt_profile: \"high-frequency targets, medium context\"\n      retnet_hurt_profile: \"long context, low-frequency targets\"\n      hgrn2_helped_profile: \"long context, high perplexity last sentence\"\n      cross_arch_feature_profile_different: true\n      cross_arch_profile_difference_p: 0.002\n    result_rationale: >\n      不同recurrence机制有不同的architectural inductive bias：\n      GDN的gated delta rule擅长precise memory update但对高频pattern可能过拟合，\n      attention介入后反而干扰了已经well-learned的高频target retrieval，导致hurt。\n      RetNet的exponential decay天然在long-range上弱，\n      attention介入后未必能完全补偿（因为attention层数有限），\n      所以long context样本被hurt。\n      HGRN2的hierarchical gating在处理high perplexity context时不够灵活，\n      attention提供了complementary的context weighting，帮助了这类样本。\n      三个architecture的feature profile显著不同（MANOVA p<0.005），\n      直接支持Claim 3：虽然aggregate convergence，但per-example mechanism是architecture-specific的。\n      3个显著features在best tier范围[2,4]内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Feature comparison of helped vs hurt samples by architecture\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"GDN Helped\", \"GDN Hurt\", \"RetNet Helped\", \"RetNet Hurt\", \"HGRN2 Helped\", \"HGRN2 Hurt\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Target freq rank (median)\", 5200, 1800, 2100, 6800, 4300, 3900]\n          - [\"Context length (mean)\", 72, 81, 58, 105, 98, 62]\n          - [\"Last-sent ppl (mean)\", 45.2, 42.8, 41.5, 48.3, 52.1, 38.7]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 6: 三个architecture的helped/hurt样本在feature space中的2D PCA投影。\n        三个panel（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2），helped为蓝色hurt为红色，\n        显示不同architecture的helped/hurt样本占据feature space的不同区域。\n      - >\n        Figure 7: Feature importance radar chart——每个architecture一个多边形，\n        显示哪些features最能区分该architecture的helped vs hurt样本。\n        三个多边形形状显著不同。\n    analysis: >\n      3个features显著区分helped/hurt（p<0.01），且feature profile跨architecture显著不同。\n      这为equalizer paradox提供了mechanistic explanation：\n      attention不是\"一刀切\"地帮助所有样本，而是根据每个architecture的specific weakness\n      修补不同类型的样本。GDN被hurt的样本恰好不是RetNet/HGRN2被hurt的样本，\n      因为三者的architectural weakness在feature space中occupies不同区域。\n      这是论文在mechanistic understanding上的核心contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      从三个architecture的hybrid models（h3-1 config, 1.3B）提取attention weight patterns，\n      分析attention focus位置、与helped/hurt sample identity的correlation、\n      cross-architecture attention pattern similarity。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_retnet: 0.31\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_hgrn2: 0.28\n      attention_pattern_similarity_retnet_hgrn2: 0.35\n      attention_helped_correlation_gdn: 0.42\n      attention_helped_correlation_retnet: 0.38\n      attention_helped_correlation_hgrn2: 0.45\n      mean_cross_arch_attention_correlation: 0.31\n      attention_focus_divergence_on_hurt_samples: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      在best tier下，attention pattern analysis将揭示：\n      (1) 三个architecture的attention层学到了不同的attention patterns（cosine similarity ~0.3），\n      因为attention层需要compensate不同的recurrence weakness，形成不同的learned strategy。\n      (2) Attention weight patterns与helped/hurt identity有moderate correlation（>0.3），\n      说明attention的\"选择性关注\"确实驱动了per-example effect。\n      GDN的attention倾向于关注distant positions（补偿delta rule的local bias），\n      RetNet的attention关注decay boundary附近的positions（补偿exponential decay的hard cutoff），\n      HGRN2的attention关注hierarchical boundary crossing的positions。\n      这些不同的compensation strategies解释了为什么affected samples不重叠。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Attention pattern analysis summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"GDN\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Mean attention entropy\", 3.21, 2.87, 3.05]\n          - [\"Dominant position (relative)\", \"distant (>50 tokens)\", \"mid-range (20-50)\", \"boundary positions\"]\n          - [\"Correlation with helped samples\", 0.42, 0.38, 0.45]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 8: Attention heatmap对比——三个architecture各一列，\n        上行为helped sample，下行为hurt sample，\n        显示attention weight分布的architecture-specific pattern。\n      - >\n        Figure 9: Attention pattern PCA——每个architecture的attention weight vectors\n        投影到2D空间，显示三个architecture形成distinct clusters。\n    analysis: >\n      Attention pattern analysis为Claim 3提供了最直接的mechanistic evidence。\n      Cross-architecture attention similarity低（~0.3）说明attention在不同architecture context中\n      学到了不同的compensation strategy，不是简单地\"添加相同的能力\"。\n      与helped/hurt的correlation > 0.3满足pass_fail标准，\n      建立了\"attention pattern → per-example effect\"的因果链条。\n      这是从descriptive到explanatory的关键升级。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索Wang et al. model zoo和其他来源的additional hybrid architectures\n      （Mamba/Mamba2 hybrids, RWKV hybrids等），评估convergence是否generalize。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 1\n      architecture_name: \"Mamba2-hybrid\"\n      mamba2_convergence_confirmed: true\n      mamba2_lambada_std_with_base: 0.027\n      mamba2_lambada_std_with_attn: 0.006\n      n_architectures_total: 4\n      convergence_holds_with_4_arch: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 2025的model zoo以GDN/RetNet/HGRN2为主，但Mamba2-hybrid\n      是近期hybrid architecture中较受关注的变体，存在已训练好的checkpoint的概率较高。\n      在best tier下，找到至少一个additional architecture并确认convergence：\n      Mamba2的selective state space mechanism与其他三种recurrence都不同，\n      但attention的equalizing effect应该仍然成立，因为attention的context integration\n      是一种general mechanism，不依赖于specific recurrence type。\n      Mamba2加入后n=4，进一步降低\"n太小\"的reviewer concern。\n      如果convergence在第四个architecture上也成立，大幅增强generalizability claim。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Extended architecture convergence\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Recurrence Type\", \"Std(h0)\", \"Std(h3-1)\", \"Reduction%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GatedDeltaNet\", \"Gated delta rule\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"Exponential decay\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"Hierarchical gating\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\"]\n          - [\"Mamba2-hybrid\", \"Selective SSM\", 0.027, 0.006, \"78%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 10 (supplementary): 四个architecture的convergence curve，\n        Mamba2用虚线标注为\"validation architecture\"，\n        与原始三个architecture的convergence趋势高度一致。\n    analysis: >\n      第四个architecture的加入将equalizer effect从\"在三个特定architecture上成立\"\n      升级为\"跨recurrence mechanism families的general phenomenon\"。\n      四种recurrence机制（delta rule, exponential decay, hierarchical gating, selective SSM）\n      代表了当前linear recurrence的主要paradigms，覆盖面足以支撑generalizability claim。\n      这直接回应Reviewer Concern D（n=3太少）。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      实现bootstrap CIs，多重比较校正，sensitivity analysis（排除GDN），\n      报告effect sizes。\n    expected_results:\n      bootstrap_ci_std_reduction_lambada: [0.014, 0.022]\n      bootstrap_ci_std_reduction_hellaswag: [0.008, 0.016]\n      bootstrap_ci_std_reduction_arc_easy: [0.012, 0.025]\n      bootstrap_ci_lower_bound_min: 0.008\n      all_cis_above_zero: true\n      bonferroni_corrected_significant_tasks: 3\n      fdr_corrected_significant_tasks: 4\n      gdn_excluded_convergence_holds: true\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_std_reduction_pct: 72\n      gdn_excluded_spearman_rho: -0.95\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 2.8\n      eta_squared_attention_effect: 0.74\n    result_rationale: >\n      在best tier下，所有statistical robustness checks通过：\n      (1) Bootstrap 95% CI lower bound > 0（最低0.008），因为convergence effect size很大（Cohen's d ~2.8），\n      即使在resampling中也不会消失。\n      (2) 排除GDN后convergence仍显著（reduction 72%），因为RetNet和HGRN2之间的convergence\n      是独立于GDN的——GDN虽有D004 confound但其removal只是略微削弱overall effect。\n      两个architecture的convergence（从std=0.018到std=0.005）本身就足够显著。\n      (3) Bonferroni校正后仍有3个任务显著，FDR校正后4个，因为原始p值足够小。\n      (4) 大effect size（η²=0.74说明74%的variance由attention ratio解释）确保statistical power充足。\n      这为所有claims提供了bulletproof的statistical foundation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Statistical robustness summary\"\n        columns: [\"Test\", \"Result\", \"Threshold\", \"Pass\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Bootstrap 95% CI (LAMBADA std reduction)\", \"[0.014, 0.022]\", \"lower > 0\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"GDN-excluded Spearman ρ\", -0.95, \"p < 0.05\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"GDN-excluded std reduction\", \"72%\", \"> 50%\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Bonferroni-corrected sig. tasks\", 3, \"≥ 2\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's d (LAMBADA)\", 2.8, \"> 0.8 (large)\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"η² (attention effect)\", 0.74, \"> 0.14 (large)\", \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 11 (supplementary): Bootstrap distribution of std reduction，\n        histogram with 95% CI marked，clearly above zero。\n      - >\n        Figure 12 (supplementary): 有/无GDN的convergence curve对比，\n        两条curve趋势一致，仅magnitude略有差异。\n    analysis: >\n      Statistical robustness framework消除了所有methodological质疑。\n      GDN exclusion test是最关键的：D004 training confound是一个已知的potential confounder，\n      但排除后核心结论不变证明convergence是三个architecture的共同现象而非GDN驱动的artifact。\n      大effect size确保即使reviewer对sample size有质疑，power analysis也站得住脚。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      系统性side-by-side对比Wang et al.的exact statements与我们的analysis，\n      量化increment。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_mentions: 2\n      wang_quantitative_convergence_metric: false\n      wang_per_example_analysis: false\n      wang_scale_dependent_analysis: false\n      wang_mechanistic_analysis: false\n      differentiation_points: 4\n      wang_quote_convergence: \"models with attention tend to perform more similarly\"\n      our_increment_summary: \"quantitative framework, scale dependency, per-example mechanism, equalizer paradox\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 2025是一篇model zoo paper，主要贡献是提供comprehensive训练和evaluation infrastructure。\n      他们在discussion中定性地提到了convergence趋势（\"models with attention tend to perform more similarly\"\n      类似措辞），但没有：(a) 计算cross-arch std trajectory——他们报告individual model performance\n      而非architecture-level variance；(b) 做per-example analysis——他们只看aggregate accuracy；\n      (c) 分析scale dependency——他们在多scale上训练但没有比较convergence across scales；\n      (d) 提出mechanistic explanation——没有分析为什么convergence发生。\n      这4个differentiation points在best tier下全部成立，因为Wang et al.的论文目标是model zoo本身\n      而非convergence现象的深入分析。我们的contribution是\"使用他们的excellent data\n      发现他们没有探索的深层现象\"，这是一种清晰的互补关系。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Contribution differentiation\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis Dimension\", \"Wang et al.\", \"Ours\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Convergence metric\", \"Qualitative mention\", \"Quantitative std trajectory + Spearman test\"]\n          - [\"Per-example analysis\", \"Not performed\", \"Helped/hurt classification + Jaccard overlap\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"Multi-scale training, no convergence analysis\", \"340M→1.3B→7B convergence curve + rebound mechanism\"]\n          - [\"Mechanistic analysis\", \"Not performed\", \"Feature characterization + attention pattern analysis\"]\n          - [\"Paradox identification\", \"Not identified\", \"Aggregate convergence + per-example divergence\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      4-point differentiation清晰建立了our contribution的independent value。\n      关键narrative：我们不是在\"重复\"Wang et al.的工作，而是在他们的data上发现了\n      他们没有寻找的deeper phenomenon。这类似于\"dataset paper\"vs\"analysis paper\"的关系。\n      Wang et al.实际上strengthen了我们的position：他们的comprehensive model zoo\n      使我们的per-example analysis更有说服力，因为models are trained under controlled conditions。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      在LAMBADA上同时绘制aggregate convergence curve和per-example divergence metrics\n      随attention ratio的变化，展示convergence和divergence的co-evolution。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation: -0.92\n      convergence_divergence_p_value: 0.003\n      co_evolution_confirmed: true\n      paradox_intensification_with_attention: true\n      max_paradox_ratio_at_h3_1: 15.8\n      paradox_ratio_definition: \"std_reduction / mean_jaccard\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在best tier下，convergence和divergence强烈anti-correlated（r=-0.92）：\n      更多attention同时带来更强的aggregate convergence和更低的per-example overlap。\n      原因：每增加一个attention层，attention有更多capacity去compensate architecture-specific weakness。\n      但因为每个architecture的weakness不同，additional attention capacity被分配到不同的sample subsets上，\n      导致per-example divergence加深。\n      这种co-evolution是equalizer paradox的核心：\n      attention越强→aggregate越similar→但per-example越不同。\n      paradox ratio（std_reduction / mean_jaccard）在h3-1达到最大值15.8，\n      意味着在最高attention ratio下paradox最为显著。\n      这个结果将成为论文的headline visualization和核心insight。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Convergence-divergence co-evolution\"\n        columns: [\"Attn Config\", \"Cross-arch Std\", \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard\", \"Paradox Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"h0 (no attn)\", 0.024, \"N/A\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"h6-1 (1 layer)\", 0.018, 0.09, 0.7]\n          - [\"h3-1 (2 layers)\", 0.012, 0.07, 1.7]\n          - [\"h2-1 (3 layers)\", 0.008, 0.05, 3.2]\n          - [\"h1-1 (4 layers)\", 0.005, 0.04, 4.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 13 (paper的hero figure): 双y轴图——左轴为cross-arch std（下降趋势），\n        右轴为mean pairwise Jaccard（也下降趋势），x轴为attention ratio。\n        两条曲线同时下降，标注\"The Equalizer Paradox\"区域。\n        shaded region表示bootstrap CI。\n      - >\n        Figure 14: Paradox ratio（std_reduction/jaccard）随attention ratio单调增加的bar chart，\n        直观展示paradox随attention加深。\n    analysis: >\n      这是论文的conceptual核心和最重要的visualization。\n      Convergence-divergence co-evolution将三条claims统一到一个coherent framework中：\n      Claim 1（aggregate convergence）+ Claim 3（per-example divergence）= Equalizer Paradox，\n      而Claim 2（scale dependency）说明这个paradox只在sufficient scale下fully emerge。\n      correlation r=-0.92 (p=0.003)提供了strong statistical evidence。\n      这个figure应该是论文的Figure 1或Figure 2，placed prominently to hook readers。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c735bf5f-f1ac-4fff-bfc2-71786796f636","uuid":"248d4d76-cbce-4a7a-a815-66f8136549c3"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":197068,"duration_api_ms":198286,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  三条claims全部保留，title直接用\"The Equalizer Effect\"。\n  叙事主线：attention作为universal equalizer跨任务跨scale生效，但per-example机制architecture-specific。\n  7B三点scale curve完成monotonic convergence story。\n  多任务覆盖（LAMBADA+HellaSwag+ARC-e）消除task-specificity质疑。\n  与Wang et al.形成清晰互补：他们提供model zoo，我们揭示他们遗漏的深层现象。\n  目标EMNLP 2026 Main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Cross-task convergence quantification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对6个benchmark在1.3B和340M两个scale上计算cross-architecture std随attention ratio变化趋势，\n      Spearman rank correlation检验convergence显著性，按retrieval-dependent vs reasoning-dependent分类。\n    expected_results:\n      tasks_with_significant_convergence_1_3b: 4\n      lambada_spearman_rho: -1.0\n      lambada_spearman_p: 0.0083\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 79\n      hellaswag_spearman_rho: -0.90\n      hellaswag_spearman_p: 0.037\n      arc_easy_spearman_rho: -0.95\n      arc_easy_spearman_p: 0.017\n      winogrande_spearman_rho: -0.90\n      winogrande_spearman_p: 0.037\n      piqa_spearman_rho: -0.50\n      piqa_spearman_p: 0.391\n      arc_challenge_spearman_rho: -0.60\n      arc_challenge_spearman_p: 0.285\n      retrieval_tasks_avg_rho: -0.94\n      reasoning_tasks_avg_rho: -0.55\n      task_type_dichotomy_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA是纯retrieval任务（从context中提取最后一词），convergence最强（ρ=-1.0）已被现有数据确认。\n      HellaSwag（commonsense continuation选择）和ARC-e（简单科学问答）均有较强的context-grounding成分，\n      attention层通过增强context integration使不同recurrence机制的弱点得到互补性修正，因此也会出现显著convergence。\n      Winogrande（共指消解）需要精确的long-range reference resolution，这恰好是attention的强项，\n      因此也会出现convergence。PIQA和ARC-challenge更依赖reasoning和world knowledge而非retrieval，\n      不同recurrence机制在这些任务上的差异更多来自训练动态而非architecture capacity gap，\n      attention无法系统性地弥合这类差异，convergence不显著。\n      这形成了清晰的task-type dichotomy：retrieval-dependent任务convergence显著，reasoning任务不显著。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Task Type\", \"Std(attn=0)\", \"Std(attn=8)\", \"Reduction%\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"retrieval\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\", -1.00, 0.0083]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"retrieval-grounded\", 0.018, 0.007, \"61%\", -0.90, 0.037]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"retrieval-grounded\", 0.031, 0.011, \"65%\", -0.95, 0.017]\n          - [\"Winogrande\", \"coreference\", 0.022, 0.009, \"59%\", -0.90, 0.037]\n          - [\"PIQA\", \"reasoning\", 0.015, 0.011, \"27%\", -0.50, 0.391]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"reasoning\", 0.028, 0.019, \"32%\", -0.60, 0.285]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 1: 六个benchmark的cross-arch std vs attention ratio折线图（1.3B），\n        retrieval类任务用实线（显示clear monotonic decrease），reasoning类用虚线（flat或noisy）。\n        双panel：左1.3B右340M，340M panel显示rebound现象。\n    analysis: >\n      4个任务显著convergence超出pass_fail阈值（≥2），且task-type dichotomy清晰。\n      retrieval-dependent任务的convergence可用attention的context integration功能解释：\n      不同recurrence机制各有retrieval盲区，attention统一补偿这些盲区。\n      reasoning任务的non-convergence支持\"equalizer effect is retrieval-specific\"的refined claim，\n      这比\"universal convergence\"更有趣——说明attention的equalizing作用有边界条件。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对1.3B模型在HellaSwag、ARC-easy、ARC-challenge上用--log_samples重新跑lm-eval，\n      提取per-example accuracy变化，计算cross-architecture helped/hurt overlap（Jaccard），\n      验证equalizer paradox是否在LAMBADA之外复现。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_mean: 0.06\n      arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_mean: 0.07\n      arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_mean: 0.12\n      hellaswag_helped_pct_gdn: 0.18\n      hellaswag_helped_pct_retnet: 0.21\n      hellaswag_helped_pct_hgrn2: 0.19\n      hellaswag_hurt_pct_gdn: 0.14\n      hellaswag_hurt_pct_retnet: 0.11\n      hellaswag_hurt_pct_hgrn2: 0.09\n      paradox_replicated_hellaswag: true\n      paradox_replicated_arc_easy: true\n      paradox_replicated_arc_challenge: false\n      gpu_hours_actual: 7.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      HellaSwag和ARC-e在exp-001中显示显著aggregate convergence，per-example分析将揭示\n      这种convergence也是通过non-overlapping sample subsets实现的（Jaccard<0.10），\n      因为不同recurrence机制的context建模弱点在不同样本上显现：\n      GDN的gated delta rule在需要precise memory update的样本上弱，\n      RetNet的exponential decay在long-range dependency样本上弱，\n      HGRN2的hierarchical gating在需要flat attention分布的样本上弱。\n      Attention分别修补这些不同的弱点，因此affected samples几乎不重叠。\n      ARC-challenge因为aggregate convergence本身不显著，per-example pattern也更noisy，\n      Jaccard略高但paradox不clean。\n      这个结果直接强化Claim 3：equalizer paradox不是LAMBADA的artifact，\n      而是retrieval-grounded任务的general phenomenon。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-example overlap across benchmarks (Jaccard index, 1.3B, h3-1 vs h0)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"GDN-RetNet\", \"GDN-HGRN2\", \"RetNet-HGRN2\", \"Mean Jaccard\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", 0.04, 0.05, 0.03, 0.04]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", 0.07, 0.06, 0.05, 0.06]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", 0.08, 0.07, 0.06, 0.07]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", 0.14, 0.11, 0.12, 0.12]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 2: 三个benchmark的Venn diagram（或UpSet plot），展示三个architecture的helped samples重叠。\n        每个benchmark一个panel，清晰显示重叠区域极小。\n      - >\n        Figure 3: Per-example effect heatmap——行为样本，列为architecture，\n        颜色编码accuracy变化方向和幅度，显示\"棋盘格\"pattern（非一致方向）。\n    analysis: >\n      Equalizer paradox在LAMBADA、HellaSwag、ARC-e三个任务上复现，\n      mean Jaccard均<0.10，满足best tier的pass_fail标准。\n      这是论文的核心contribution加强版：paradox不是task-specific artifact，\n      而是attention介入retrieval-dependent任务的general mechanism。\n      ARC-challenge的higher Jaccard提供了有趣的boundary condition讨论。\n\n  - name: \"7B model evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      从Wang et al. HuggingFace repos获取7B-scale models，\n      在6个benchmark上评估，构建3-scale (340M, 1.3B, 7B) convergence trajectory。\n    expected_results:\n      models_available_7b: 3\n      architectures_available_7b: [\"GatedDeltaNet\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_7b_h0: 0.019\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_7b_h3_1: 0.002\n      lambada_std_reduction_7b_pct: 89\n      hellaswag_std_reduction_7b_pct: 75\n      arc_easy_std_reduction_7b_pct: 71\n      scale_convergence_spearman_rho: -1.0\n      scale_convergence_spearman_p: 0.0083\n      monotonic_deepening_confirmed: true\n      gpu_hours_actual: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al.的model zoo包含多scale实验，7B是他们的largest scale，极可能有模型。\n      在best tier下，7B模型可获取且convergence继续deepening的原因：\n      (1) 更大的模型capacity使attention层的context integration更充分，\n      各recurrence机制的residual差异被更有效地弥合；\n      (2) 7B的training dynamics更稳定，340M的rebound现象（capacity不足导致attention和recurrence争抢参数）\n      在7B上消失；\n      (3) 三点scale curve (340M partial → 1.3B strong → 7B near-complete)\n      形成clean monotonic trajectory，std reduction从~40% → ~79% → ~89%，\n      支持\"convergence随scale增强\"的narrative。\n      这完成了Claim 2的scale story，从binary contrast升级为三点趋势线。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Cross-architecture std across scales\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"Attn Config\", \"LAMBADA Std\", \"HellaSwag Std\", \"ARC-E Std\", \"Mean Std (retrieval tasks)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"340M\", \"h0\", 0.021, 0.016, 0.028, 0.022]\n          - [\"340M\", \"h3-1\", 0.013, 0.012, 0.020, 0.015]\n          - [\"1.3B\", \"h0\", 0.024, 0.018, 0.031, 0.024]\n          - [\"1.3B\", \"h3-1\", 0.005, 0.007, 0.011, 0.008]\n          - [\"7B\", \"h0\", 0.019, 0.015, 0.025, 0.020]\n          - [\"7B\", \"h3-1\", 0.002, 0.004, 0.007, 0.004]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4: 三点scale curve——x轴为model scale (340M, 1.3B, 7B)，\n        y轴为cross-arch std (h3-1 config)，三条线分别对应LAMBADA、HellaSwag、ARC-e。\n        所有线monotonically decrease，LAMBADA下降最陡。\n        右侧secondary y轴显示std reduction percentage。\n    analysis: >\n      7B数据的获取和monotonic deepening是best tier的关键区分因素。\n      三点curve使Claim 2从\"two-point contrast\"升级为\"scaling law\"，\n      可以拟合power law或log-linear关系，增强理论深度。\n      7B的near-complete convergence（LAMBADA std仅0.002）暗示\n      在sufficient scale下attention几乎完全消除architecture差异，\n      这对architecture selection有直接practical implication。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析340M在attn=8时的non-monotonic rebound，\n      per-example比较340M和1.3B在相同attention ratio下的差异，\n      识别rebound的根本原因。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_magnitude_std_increase: 0.006\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 0.45\n      capacity_bottleneck_confirmed: true\n      rebound_correlated_with_context_length: true\n      rebound_context_length_threshold: 85\n      rebound_explained_variance_by_capacity: 0.62\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M的rebound在attn=8时出现，这是最高attention ratio。\n      在best tier下，机制将被清晰识别为capacity bottleneck：\n      340M总参数有限，当attention层占比过高时recurrence层的参数被过度压缩，\n      导致recurrence的sequence modeling能力退化。\n      表现为长context样本（>85 tokens）上的性能下降，\n      因为这些样本本来最依赖recurrence的sequential processing。\n      1.3B不出现rebound是因为总capacity足够同时支撑attention和recurrence。\n      这个发现完美补充scale story：convergence需要sufficient scale，\n      不仅是scale越大convergence越深，而且scale不足时会出现pathological behavior。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: 340M rebound characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Rebound Samples\", \"Non-rebound Samples\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Mean context length (tokens)\", 112.3, 68.7, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"Target token frequency rank\", 4521, 3890, 0.23]\n          - [\"Overlap with 1.3B hurt samples\", \"45%\", \"12%\", \"<0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 5: 340M vs 1.3B的per-example effect scatter plot，\n        x轴为1.3B上的accuracy change，y轴为340M上的accuracy change。\n        颜色编码context length，长context样本聚集在340M negative / 1.3B positive象限。\n    analysis: >\n      Capacity bottleneck解释简洁且可验证，为scale-dependent convergence提供mechanistic grounding。\n      长context样本在340M上的rebound可以解释为：recurrence层capacity不足以维持long-range state，\n      而attention层虽然能做long-range retrieval但在340M上head数量不足以覆盖所有位置。\n      这个发现增加了论文的理论深度，不仅是描述性的\"scale matters\"，而是解释性的\"why scale matters\"。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对LAMBADA上每个architecture的helped/hurt samples计算linguistic features：\n      target token frequency, context length, last-sentence perplexity, topic distribution，\n      检验feature是否显著区分helped vs hurt，以及feature profile是否跨architecture不同。\n    expected_results:\n      significant_features_count: 3\n      target_token_frequency_p_value: 0.003\n      context_length_p_value: 0.001\n      last_sentence_perplexity_p_value: 0.008\n      topic_distribution_p_value: 0.12\n      gdn_hurt_profile: \"high-frequency targets, medium context\"\n      retnet_hurt_profile: \"long context, low-frequency targets\"\n      hgrn2_helped_profile: \"long context, high perplexity last sentence\"\n      cross_arch_feature_profile_different: true\n      cross_arch_profile_difference_p: 0.002\n    result_rationale: >\n      不同recurrence机制有不同的architectural inductive bias：\n      GDN的gated delta rule擅长precise memory update但对高频pattern可能过拟合，\n      attention介入后反而干扰了已经well-learned的高频target retrieval，导致hurt。\n      RetNet的exponential decay天然在long-range上弱，\n      attention介入后未必能完全补偿（因为attention层数有限），\n      所以long context样本被hurt。\n      HGRN2的hierarchical gating在处理high perplexity context时不够灵活，\n      attention提供了complementary的context weighting，帮助了这类样本。\n      三个architecture的feature profile显著不同（MANOVA p<0.005），\n      直接支持Claim 3：虽然aggregate convergence，但per-example mechanism是architecture-specific的。\n      3个显著features在best tier范围[2,4]内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Feature comparison of helped vs hurt samples by architecture\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"GDN Helped\", \"GDN Hurt\", \"RetNet Helped\", \"RetNet Hurt\", \"HGRN2 Helped\", \"HGRN2 Hurt\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Target freq rank (median)\", 5200, 1800, 2100, 6800, 4300, 3900]\n          - [\"Context length (mean)\", 72, 81, 58, 105, 98, 62]\n          - [\"Last-sent ppl (mean)\", 45.2, 42.8, 41.5, 48.3, 52.1, 38.7]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 6: 三个architecture的helped/hurt样本在feature space中的2D PCA投影。\n        三个panel（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2），helped为蓝色hurt为红色，\n        显示不同architecture的helped/hurt样本占据feature space的不同区域。\n      - >\n        Figure 7: Feature importance radar chart——每个architecture一个多边形，\n        显示哪些features最能区分该architecture的helped vs hurt样本。\n        三个多边形形状显著不同。\n    analysis: >\n      3个features显著区分helped/hurt（p<0.01），且feature profile跨architecture显著不同。\n      这为equalizer paradox提供了mechanistic explanation：\n      attention不是\"一刀切\"地帮助所有样本，而是根据每个architecture的specific weakness\n      修补不同类型的样本。GDN被hurt的样本恰好不是RetNet/HGRN2被hurt的样本，\n      因为三者的architectural weakness在feature space中occupies不同区域。\n      这是论文在mechanistic understanding上的核心contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      从三个architecture的hybrid models（h3-1 config, 1.3B）提取attention weight patterns，\n      分析attention focus位置、与helped/hurt sample identity的correlation、\n      cross-architecture attention pattern similarity。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_retnet: 0.31\n      attention_pattern_similarity_gdn_hgrn2: 0.28\n      attention_pattern_similarity_retnet_hgrn2: 0.35\n      attention_helped_correlation_gdn: 0.42\n      attention_helped_correlation_retnet: 0.38\n      attention_helped_correlation_hgrn2: 0.45\n      mean_cross_arch_attention_correlation: 0.31\n      attention_focus_divergence_on_hurt_samples: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      在best tier下，attention pattern analysis将揭示：\n      (1) 三个architecture的attention层学到了不同的attention patterns（cosine similarity ~0.3），\n      因为attention层需要compensate不同的recurrence weakness，形成不同的learned strategy。\n      (2) Attention weight patterns与helped/hurt identity有moderate correlation（>0.3），\n      说明attention的\"选择性关注\"确实驱动了per-example effect。\n      GDN的attention倾向于关注distant positions（补偿delta rule的local bias），\n      RetNet的attention关注decay boundary附近的positions（补偿exponential decay的hard cutoff），\n      HGRN2的attention关注hierarchical boundary crossing的positions。\n      这些不同的compensation strategies解释了为什么affected samples不重叠。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Attention pattern analysis summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"GDN\", \"RetNet\", \"HGRN2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Mean attention entropy\", 3.21, 2.87, 3.05]\n          - [\"Dominant position (relative)\", \"distant (>50 tokens)\", \"mid-range (20-50)\", \"boundary positions\"]\n          - [\"Correlation with helped samples\", 0.42, 0.38, 0.45]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 8: Attention heatmap对比——三个architecture各一列，\n        上行为helped sample，下行为hurt sample，\n        显示attention weight分布的architecture-specific pattern。\n      - >\n        Figure 9: Attention pattern PCA——每个architecture的attention weight vectors\n        投影到2D空间，显示三个architecture形成distinct clusters。\n    analysis: >\n      Attention pattern analysis为Claim 3提供了最直接的mechanistic evidence。\n      Cross-architecture attention similarity低（~0.3）说明attention在不同architecture context中\n      学到了不同的compensation strategy，不是简单地\"添加相同的能力\"。\n      与helped/hurt的correlation > 0.3满足pass_fail标准，\n      建立了\"attention pattern → per-example effect\"的因果链条。\n      这是从descriptive到explanatory的关键升级。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索Wang et al. model zoo和其他来源的additional hybrid architectures\n      （Mamba/Mamba2 hybrids, RWKV hybrids等），评估convergence是否generalize。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 1\n      architecture_name: \"Mamba2-hybrid\"\n      mamba2_convergence_confirmed: true\n      mamba2_lambada_std_with_base: 0.027\n      mamba2_lambada_std_with_attn: 0.006\n      n_architectures_total: 4\n      convergence_holds_with_4_arch: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 2025的model zoo以GDN/RetNet/HGRN2为主，但Mamba2-hybrid\n      是近期hybrid architecture中较受关注的变体，存在已训练好的checkpoint的概率较高。\n      在best tier下，找到至少一个additional architecture并确认convergence：\n      Mamba2的selective state space mechanism与其他三种recurrence都不同，\n      但attention的equalizing effect应该仍然成立，因为attention的context integration\n      是一种general mechanism，不依赖于specific recurrence type。\n      Mamba2加入后n=4，进一步降低\"n太小\"的reviewer concern。\n      如果convergence在第四个architecture上也成立，大幅增强generalizability claim。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Extended architecture convergence\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Recurrence Type\", \"Std(h0)\", \"Std(h3-1)\", \"Reduction%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GatedDeltaNet\", \"Gated delta rule\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"Exponential decay\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"Hierarchical gating\", 0.024, 0.005, \"79%\"]\n          - [\"Mamba2-hybrid\", \"Selective SSM\", 0.027, 0.006, \"78%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 10 (supplementary): 四个architecture的convergence curve，\n        Mamba2用虚线标注为\"validation architecture\"，\n        与原始三个architecture的convergence趋势高度一致。\n    analysis: >\n      第四个architecture的加入将equalizer effect从\"在三个特定architecture上成立\"\n      升级为\"跨recurrence mechanism families的general phenomenon\"。\n      四种recurrence机制（delta rule, exponential decay, hierarchical gating, selective SSM）\n      代表了当前linear recurrence的主要paradigms，覆盖面足以支撑generalizability claim。\n      这直接回应Reviewer Concern D（n=3太少）。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      实现bootstrap CIs，多重比较校正，sensitivity analysis（排除GDN），\n      报告effect sizes。\n    expected_results:\n      bootstrap_ci_std_reduction_lambada: [0.014, 0.022]\n      bootstrap_ci_std_reduction_hellaswag: [0.008, 0.016]\n      bootstrap_ci_std_reduction_arc_easy: [0.012, 0.025]\n      bootstrap_ci_lower_bound_min: 0.008\n      all_cis_above_zero: true\n      bonferroni_corrected_significant_tasks: 3\n      fdr_corrected_significant_tasks: 4\n      gdn_excluded_convergence_holds: true\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_std_reduction_pct: 72\n      gdn_excluded_spearman_rho: -0.95\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 2.8\n      eta_squared_attention_effect: 0.74\n    result_rationale: >\n      在best tier下，所有statistical robustness checks通过：\n      (1) Bootstrap 95% CI lower bound > 0（最低0.008），因为convergence effect size很大（Cohen's d ~2.8），\n      即使在resampling中也不会消失。\n      (2) 排除GDN后convergence仍显著（reduction 72%），因为RetNet和HGRN2之间的convergence\n      是独立于GDN的——GDN虽有D004 confound但其removal只是略微削弱overall effect。\n      两个architecture的convergence（从std=0.018到std=0.005）本身就足够显著。\n      (3) Bonferroni校正后仍有3个任务显著，FDR校正后4个，因为原始p值足够小。\n      (4) 大effect size（η²=0.74说明74%的variance由attention ratio解释）确保statistical power充足。\n      这为所有claims提供了bulletproof的statistical foundation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Statistical robustness summary\"\n        columns: [\"Test\", \"Result\", \"Threshold\", \"Pass\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Bootstrap 95% CI (LAMBADA std reduction)\", \"[0.014, 0.022]\", \"lower > 0\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"GDN-excluded Spearman ρ\", -0.95, \"p < 0.05\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"GDN-excluded std reduction\", \"72%\", \"> 50%\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Bonferroni-corrected sig. tasks\", 3, \"≥ 2\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's d (LAMBADA)\", 2.8, \"> 0.8 (large)\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"η² (attention effect)\", 0.74, \"> 0.14 (large)\", \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 11 (supplementary): Bootstrap distribution of std reduction，\n        histogram with 95% CI marked，clearly above zero。\n      - >\n        Figure 12 (supplementary): 有/无GDN的convergence curve对比，\n        两条curve趋势一致，仅magnitude略有差异。\n    analysis: >\n      Statistical robustness framework消除了所有methodological质疑。\n      GDN exclusion test是最关键的：D004 training confound是一个已知的potential confounder，\n      但排除后核心结论不变证明convergence是三个architecture的共同现象而非GDN驱动的artifact。\n      大effect size确保即使reviewer对sample size有质疑，power analysis也站得住脚。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      系统性side-by-side对比Wang et al.的exact statements与我们的analysis，\n      量化increment。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_mentions: 2\n      wang_quantitative_convergence_metric: false\n      wang_per_example_analysis: false\n      wang_scale_dependent_analysis: false\n      wang_mechanistic_analysis: false\n      differentiation_points: 4\n      wang_quote_convergence: \"models with attention tend to perform more similarly\"\n      our_increment_summary: \"quantitative framework, scale dependency, per-example mechanism, equalizer paradox\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 2025是一篇model zoo paper，主要贡献是提供comprehensive训练和evaluation infrastructure。\n      他们在discussion中定性地提到了convergence趋势（\"models with attention tend to perform more similarly\"\n      类似措辞），但没有：(a) 计算cross-arch std trajectory——他们报告individual model performance\n      而非architecture-level variance；(b) 做per-example analysis——他们只看aggregate accuracy；\n      (c) 分析scale dependency——他们在多scale上训练但没有比较convergence across scales；\n      (d) 提出mechanistic explanation——没有分析为什么convergence发生。\n      这4个differentiation points在best tier下全部成立，因为Wang et al.的论文目标是model zoo本身\n      而非convergence现象的深入分析。我们的contribution是\"使用他们的excellent data\n      发现他们没有探索的深层现象\"，这是一种清晰的互补关系。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Contribution differentiation\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis Dimension\", \"Wang et al.\", \"Ours\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Convergence metric\", \"Qualitative mention\", \"Quantitative std trajectory + Spearman test\"]\n          - [\"Per-example analysis\", \"Not performed\", \"Helped/hurt classification + Jaccard overlap\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"Multi-scale training, no convergence analysis\", \"340M→1.3B→7B convergence curve + rebound mechanism\"]\n          - [\"Mechanistic analysis\", \"Not performed\", \"Feature characterization + attention pattern analysis\"]\n          - [\"Paradox identification\", \"Not identified\", \"Aggregate convergence + per-example divergence\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      4-point differentiation清晰建立了our contribution的independent value。\n      关键narrative：我们不是在\"重复\"Wang et al.的工作，而是在他们的data上发现了\n      他们没有寻找的deeper phenomenon。这类似于\"dataset paper\"vs\"analysis paper\"的关系。\n      Wang et al.实际上strengthen了我们的position：他们的comprehensive model zoo\n      使我们的per-example analysis更有说服力，因为models are trained under controlled conditions。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      在LAMBADA上同时绘制aggregate convergence curve和per-example divergence metrics\n      随attention ratio的变化，展示convergence和divergence的co-evolution。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation: -0.92\n      convergence_divergence_p_value: 0.003\n      co_evolution_confirmed: true\n      paradox_intensification_with_attention: true\n      max_paradox_ratio_at_h3_1: 15.8\n      paradox_ratio_definition: \"std_reduction / mean_jaccard\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在best tier下，convergence和divergence强烈anti-correlated（r=-0.92）：\n      更多attention同时带来更强的aggregate convergence和更低的per-example overlap。\n      原因：每增加一个attention层，attention有更多capacity去compensate architecture-specific weakness。\n      但因为每个architecture的weakness不同，additional attention capacity被分配到不同的sample subsets上，\n      导致per-example divergence加深。\n      这种co-evolution是equalizer paradox的核心：\n      attention越强→aggregate越similar→但per-example越不同。\n      paradox ratio（std_reduction / mean_jaccard）在h3-1达到最大值15.8，\n      意味着在最高attention ratio下paradox最为显著。\n      这个结果将成为论文的headline visualization和核心insight。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Convergence-divergence co-evolution\"\n        columns: [\"Attn Config\", \"Cross-arch Std\", \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard\", \"Paradox Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"h0 (no attn)\", 0.024, \"N/A\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"h6-1 (1 layer)\", 0.018, 0.09, 0.7]\n          - [\"h3-1 (2 layers)\", 0.012, 0.07, 1.7]\n          - [\"h2-1 (3 layers)\", 0.008, 0.05, 3.2]\n          - [\"h1-1 (4 layers)\", 0.005, 0.04, 4.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 13 (paper的hero figure): 双y轴图——左轴为cross-arch std（下降趋势），\n        右轴为mean pairwise Jaccard（也下降趋势），x轴为attention ratio。\n        两条曲线同时下降，标注\"The Equalizer Paradox\"区域。\n        shaded region表示bootstrap CI。\n      - >\n        Figure 14: Paradox ratio（std_reduction/jaccard）随attention ratio单调增加的bar chart，\n        直观展示paradox随attention加深。\n    analysis: >\n      这是论文的conceptual核心和最重要的visualization。\n      Convergence-divergence co-evolution将三条claims统一到一个coherent framework中：\n      Claim 1（aggregate convergence）+ Claim 3（per-example divergence）= Equalizer Paradox，\n      而Claim 2（scale dependency）说明这个paradox只在sufficient scale下fully emerge。\n      correlation r=-0.92 (p=0.003)提供了strong statistical evidence。\n      这个figure应该是论文的Figure 1或Figure 2，placed prominently to hook readers。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c735bf5f-f1ac-4fff-bfc2-71786796f636","total_cost_usd":0.31627125,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":9837,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"